# serializer version: 1
# name: TestClassifyMessageIsAgentDirected.test_prompt_snapshot_matches
  '''
  The PostHog agent is working on a task in this Slack thread. People in the thread have stopped tagging it. Decide whether the latest message is an instruction to the agent that happens to omit the @mention.
  
  Answer true only when the message is addressed to the agent:
    - An order or request to do something ('also handle the empty case', 'skip the migration', 'open a PR for that too', 'try again with the other helper').
    - A question put to the agent about its own work ('why did you skip the redesign commit?', 'does your PR cover the mobile breakpoint?').
    - An answer to something the agent just asked in this thread.
    - A correction of what the agent said or did ('no, the bug is in the handler, not the wrapper').
  
  Answer false for everything else. This is the common case, and the mistake to avoid — people talk about the work far more often than they talk to the agent:
    - Opinions and discussion about the task or the product, addressed to the room ('this needs a stronger label', 'it should probably live under settings', 'I've seen this set back and forth so much'). Relevant to the task is not the same as addressed to the agent.
    - Talk about the agent in the third person ('why is the bot reacting to me?', 'it keeps replying', 'is it supposed to do that?'). Being the topic is not being the audience.
    - Conversation between humans — answering each other, tagging each other, deciding something among themselves.
    - Acknowledgements, praise, and reactions ('thanks', 'lgtm', 'nice', '+1').
    - Context dropped into the thread with no instruction attached — a link, a stack trace, a screenshot — unless the message asks the agent to act on it.
    - Anything off-topic.
  
  When you are unsure, answer false. A missed instruction costs the author one @PostHog; a wrong wake-up makes the agent interrupt a conversation it was not part of, in public, where everyone sees it.
  
  Task the agent is working on: Fix the checkout button not firing autocapture events
  
  Thread so far (oldest first):
  alice: @PostHog autocapture isn't picking up clicks on our checkout button
  posthog: Looking into it — checking how the button is rendered.
  
  Latest message (from a human in this thread): this whole thing would benefit from a Settings section
  
  Answer with the one field, e.g. {"agent_directed": false}
  '''
# ---
